    "lawCode": "Rpld §216 sub 2 ¶ b, rpld & add §216 sub 2 ¶ a, rpld & add §216-c sub 2, rpld §216-b sub 5 ¶¶ (b), (c) & (d), add ¶¶ (b) & (c), Exec L; rpld & add §207-b sub 2 ¶ b, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5504\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\nterms and conditions of employment for members of the collective\nnegotiating unit consisting of investigators, senior investigators,\nand investigative specialists in the division of state police; to\namend the state finance law, in relation to terms and conditions of\nemployment for members of the collective negotiating unit consisting\nof investigators, senior investigators, and investigative specialists\nin the division of state police; in relation to implementing an\nagreement covering such members of such unit and in relation to the\nemployee benefit fund for members of such unit; to amend the executive\nlaw, in relation to salary schedules for such members of such unit;\nmaking an appropriation therefor; and to repeal certain provisions of\nsuch laws relating thereto\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would implement the provisions of a collective bargaining\nagreement between the Executive Branch of the State of New York and\nthe employee organization which represents members of the collective\nnegotiating unit consisting of investigators, senior investigators and\ninvestigative specialists in the Division of State Police (hereinafter\n\"members of the BCI unit\").\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would repeal Executive Law § 216(2)(b), which\nestablished a salary schedule for members of the commissioned and\nnon-commissioned officers unit in the Division of State Police for the\nyears 1991 through 1994. Such salary schedule is now found in\nExecutive Law § 215.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would repeal Executive Law § 216(2)(a) and\nreplace it with a new paragraph establishing a new salary schedule for\nmembers of the BCI unit. Basic annual salaries for such members will\nincrease by 3 percent, effective April 1, 2007; by 3 percent,\neffective April 1, 2008; by 3 percent, effective April 1, 2009, and by\n4 percent, effective April 1, 2010. This section also establishes a\nnew salary schedule for such members, effective March 31, 2011, which\nrolls command pay and premium pay into base salary.\n\nSection 3 of the bill would repeal State Finance Law § 207-b(2)(b) and\nreplace it with a new paragraph that continues payments to the\nEmployee Benefit Fund for members of the BCI unit. Under this\nprovision, the Employee Benefit Fund payment will continue at $49 per\nmember, per year for the period April 1, 2007 to March 31, 2011.\n\nSection 4 of the bill would repeal Executive Law § 216-c(2) and\nreplace it with a new subdivision that continues holiday payments that\nwill increase by the same percentage increases as applied to basic\nannual salaries in section 2 of this bill. Effective April 1, 2007,\nsuch amount will increase to $1392. Effective April 1, 2008, such\namount will increase to $1434. Effective April 1, 2009, such amount\nwill increase to $1477. Effective April 1, 2010, such amount will\nincrease to $1536.\n\nSection 5 of the bill would repeal Executive Law §§ 216-b(5)(b), (c)\nand (d) and replace them with new subdivisions (b) and (c), which\nwould provide for a new longevity award schedule for members of the\nBCI unit, as follows: Effective April 1, 2007: (a) 6 to 10 years of\nservice - $430; (b) 11 to 15 years of service - $480; and (c) 16 to 25\nyears of service - $530. Effective April 1, 2008, such amounts will\nincrease to $460, $510, and $560, respectively. Effective April 1,\n2009, such amounts will increase to $500, $550, $600, respectively.\n\nEffective April 1, 2010, such amounts increase to $540, $590, and\n$640, respectively.\n\nSection 6 of the bill would provide an increase to the premium in lieu\nof overtime paid to senior investigators, increasing such overtime\npremium by the same percentage increases as applied to basic annual\nsalaries in section 2 of this bill, to the amount of $10,818,\neffective April 1, 2007, to the amount of $11,143, effective April 1,\n2008, to the amount of $11,477, effective April 1, 2009 and to the\namount of $11,936, effective April 1, 2010. Effective March 31, 2011,\nsuch premium will be rolled into base salary.\n\nSection 7 of the bill would provide an increase in the command pay\nprovided to senior investigators of the BCI unit, increasing such pay\nby the same percentage increases as applied to basic annual salaries\nin section 2 of this bill, to the amount of $2,699, effective April 1,\n2007, to the amount of $2,780, effective April 1, 2008, to the amount\nof $2,863, effective April 1, 2009 and to the amount of $2,978,\neffective April 1, 2010. Effective March 31, 2011, such command pay\nwill be rolled into base salary.\n\nSection 8 of the bill would continue funding for the committee on\nhealth benefits in the amount of $5,000 per year during the period\nApril 1, 2007 through March 31, 2011.\n\nSection 9 of the bill would provide for an increase in the maintenance\nallowance for members of the BCI unit, increasing such allowance by\nthe same percentage increases as applied to basic annual salaries in\nsection 2 of this bill, to the amount of $2,865, effective April 1,\n2007, to the amount of $2,951, effective April 1, 2008, to the amount\nof $3,040, effective April 1, 2009 and to the amount of $3,162,\neffective April 1, 2010.\n\nSection 10 of the bill would establish an annual payment of $1200,\neffective April 1, 2010, for members of the BCI unit in recognition of\nthe professional expertise of such members.\n\nSection 11 of the bill would continue funding for the professional\ndevelopment and quality of working life committee in the amount of\n$81,900 during the period April 1, 2007 to March 31, 2011, to provide\nsupport for the advanced degree educational opportunity program, the\ntuition reimbursement program and the employee assistance program.\n\nSection 12 of the bill would provide for an annual $1200 increase in\nexpanded duty pay for members of the BCI unit, to the amount of\n$3,852, effective April 1, 2007; to the amount of $5,052, effective\nApril 1, 2008, to the amount of $6,252, effective April 1, 2009 and to\nthe amount of $7,452, effective April 1, 2010, in recognition of such\nmembers' expanded duties related to counterterrorism, computer crimes,\nand law enforcement activities involving gambling regulation.\n\nSection 13 of the bill would continue supervisory responsibility pay\nin accordance with the terms of an interest arbitration award dated\nFebruary 4, 2005, issued pursuant to Civil Service Law §209(4), for\nmembers of the BCI unit designated as \"Unit Coordinators\", \"Acting\nSenior Investigators\" or \"Acting Administrative Senior Investigators.\"\n\nSection 14 of the bill would continue the location pay benefit of $200\nfor members of the BCI unit whose official workstation is Monroe\nCounty and would increase the location pay benefit provided to members\nwhose official workstation is in New York City, or in the counties of\nRockland, Westchester, Nassau or Suffolk by the same percentage\nincreases as applied to basic annual salaries in section 2 of this\nbill.  Effective April 1, 2007, such location pay will increase to\n$1,392.  Effective April 1, 2008, such pay will increase to $1,434.\n\nEffective April 1, 2009, such pay will increase to $1,477. Effective\nApril 1, 2010, such pay will increase to $1,536.\n\nSection 15 of the bill would increase the supplemental location pay\nbenefit, as follows: Effective April 1, 2007 members of such units who\nwork in (a) Orange, Putnam or Dutchess would receive $1,160, (b)\nRockland or Westchester County or the City of New York would receive $\n1,739, and (c) in Nassau or Suffolk County would receive $2,029.\nEffective April 1, 2008, these amounts would increase to $1,195,\n$1,791, and $2,090, respectively. Effective April 1, 2009, these\namounts would increase to $1,230, $1,845, and $2,153, respectively.\nEffective April 1, 2010, these amounts would increase to $1,280,\n$1,918, and $2,239, respectively.\n\nSection 16 of the bill would continue lump sum payments for unused\nsick leave at retirement. Effective April 1, 1998, unused sick days\nwill be cashed out according to the following formula: the number of\naccumulated and unused sick days, not to exceed 300, will be reduced\nby 165 with the result being multiplied by the member's daily rate of\npay. The lump sum payable will be equal to one-fifth of such amount.\n\nSection 17 of the bill would continue the committee to study and\nassess physical fitness standards for members of the BCI unit and the\nannual appropriation for that purpose. Effective April 1, 2001,\nmembers of the BCI unit would receive a fitness bonus if they were\nfound to be eligible against established standards. The Division of\nState Police and the employee organization representing such unit may\nagree to expend the funds appropriated on an annual basis for the\nphysical fitness program for a mutually agreeable alternate purpose.\n\nSection 18 of the bill would continue a payment to members of the BCI\nunit who possess or obtain a recognized degree. Such members shall\ncontinue to receive a lump sum payment of $250 for an Associate's\nDegree, $500 for a Bachelor's Degree, and $750 for a graduate degree.\n\nSection 19 of the bill would provide that appropriations contained\ntherein shall be available to the state for the payment and\npublication of grievance arbitration settlements and awards.\n\nSection 20 of the bill would provide the date on which members of the\nBCI unit would be entitled to the salary increases provided by this\nbill.\n\nSection 21 of the bill would provide that until payment is made\npursuant to this bill, members of the BCI unit shall receive payment\notherwise payable in their respective positions. When basic annual\nsalaries are first paid pursuant to this bill, such members shall be\nentitled to a lump sum payment for the difference between the salaries\nto which they were entitled since April 1, 2007 and the compensation\nactually received.\n\nSection 22 of the bill would authorize the Comptroller to pay any\namounts required by the bill. To the extent that existing\nappropriations available to any state department or agency are\ninsufficient to accomplish the purposes set forth in this section, the\nDirector of the Budget would be authorized to allocate to the various\ndepartments and agencies the amounts necessary to make such payments.\n\nSection 23 of the bill would appropriate monies to pay for personal\nservices, other than personal services and fringe benefits, and to\ncarry out the provisions of this act.\n\nSection 24 of the bill would provide that the bill take effect\nimmediately and be deemed to have been in full force and effect on and\nafter April 1, 2007.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nChapter 112 of the Laws of 2006 and Chapter 103 of the Laws of 2005\naddress a variety of terms and conditions of employment for\ninvestigators and senior investigators established by previous\ninterest arbitration awards, and cover the period April 1, 2003 to\nMarch 31, 2007.\n\nExecutive Law §216 establishes the current salary schedules for\nmembers of the BCI unit.\n\nExecutive Law §216-b establishes the current longevity schedule for\nmembers of the BCI unit.\n\nExecutive Law §216-c establishes the current holiday pay benefit for\nmembers of the BCI unit.\n\nState Finance Law §207-b authorizes payments to an employee benefit\nfund on behalf of members of the BCI unit under interest arbitration\naward and agreement.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY : None.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nThis bill is necessary to implement the terms of a collective\nbargaining agreement negotiated between the Executive Branch of the\nState of New York and the employee organization representing members\nof the BCI unit.\n\n BUDGET IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThis bill would provide appropriations totaling approximately $43.61\nmillion (General Fund of approximately $40.20 million) to pay for the\ncost of the agreement during the period April 1, 2007 to March 31,\n2009.  The 2009-10 financial plan accommodates the costs associated\nwith this bill.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThe bill would take effect immediately and would be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect on and after April 1, 2007.\n",
